.\" Man page for portscope-cli.
.TH PORTSCOPE-CLI 1 "2026-10-22" "portscope 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portscope-cli \- reproducible diagnostic snapshots for PortScope
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portscope-cli
.RI [ snapshot " [\-\-json " PATH "]]"
.br
.B portscope-cli
.B journal
.RI [ UNIT ]
.RI [ system | user ]
.br
.B portscope-cli compare-backends
.br
.B portscope-cli \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portscope-cli
exposes the data collection used by the graphical application so that
diagnostics can be scripted and reproduced without a display server. It is the
same code path the application uses.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B snapshot
Collect endpoints, processes, services and their associations, and print a
summary. Errors are listed by their stable machine code.
.TP
.BI "snapshot \-\-json " PATH
Additionally write the complete snapshot as JSON to
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI journal " [UNIT] [SCOPE]"
Query recent journal entries, optionally filtered to one unit. The outcome is
reported as one of
.BR entries ,
.BR EMPTY ,
.B DENIED
or an error, because
.B journalctl
exits with status 0 for permission denial, an empty result and a malformed
query alike; the outcome is therefore decided from its output, not its exit
status.
.TP
.B compare-backends
Cross-check systemd unit state and cost between the D-Bus and
.B systemctl
backends. Any disagreement is a defect and causes a non-zero exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A query failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B portscope-cli snapshot \-\-json /tmp/snapshot.json
Capture a snapshot for a bug report.
.TP
.B portscope-cli journal ssh.service system
Show recent entries for a system unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR portscope (1),
.BR ss (8),
.BR journalctl (1)
